  "database": "rschema_0347",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0347 database is designed to store and manage metadata related to machine learning models and their associated datasets. The database consists of 12 tables that work together to provide a comprehensive view of the models, their performance, and the datasets they are trained on. The leaderboard_metadata table stores information about each model run, including the run ID, model execution time, start and end times, run time, run path, maximum models, and model species. The leaderboard table contains details about each model, such as its ID, name, root mean squared error (RMSE), mean squared error (MSE), mean absolute error (MAE), root mean squared log error (RMSLE), and presence stacked ensemble best of family. The model_map table maps model types to their corresponding names, while the dataset_variable_details table stores information about the variables in each dataset, including their names, data types, unique and null values, and the dataset ID they belong to. The tags table stores unique tags, and the hyperparameter_value table links models to their hyperparameters and their corresponding values. The model_run table associates model runs with their corresponding models, and the data_map table links datasets to their associated model runs. The hyperparameter_def_values table stores default values for hyperparameters based on model types, and the id_map table maps model IDs to their corresponding model types. The hyperparameter table stores unique hyperparameters, and the dataset_metadata table contains metadata about each dataset, including its ID, name, owner, license, visibility, URL, creation and last update dates, data size, number of rows, and number of columns. The relationships between these tables are established through foreign keys, which ensure data consistency and integrity, such as the cascade delete and update rules that ensure that related data is deleted or updated when a parent record is modified or deleted.",
  "gold_question": "A machine learning model management and evaluation system is used to record and manage the operational status, performance metrics, hyperparameter settings, and dataset information of various machine learning models. The requirements analysis is as follows:\nModel Run Records: Records the run ID, execution time, start time, end time, runtime, run path, maximum number of models, and model types for each model, implemented through the Leaderboard_Metadata table.\nModel Performance Evaluation: Records the ID, name, performance metrics (such as RMSE, MSE, MAE, RMSLE), and whether the best family model of stacked ensemble exists for each model, implemented through the Leaderboard table.\nHyperparameter Management: Records the ID and name of hyperparameters, implemented through the Hyperparameter table, and records the hyperparameter values for each model, implemented through the Hyperparameter_Values table.\nModel-Run Association: Records the association between each model and its run, implemented through the Model_Run table.\nDataset Management: Records the ID, name, owner, license, visibility, URL, creation date, last update date, data size, number of rows, and number of columns for each dataset, implemented through the Dataset_Metadata table.\nDataset-Run Association: Records the association between each dataset and its run, implemented through the Data_Map table.\nModel Type Management: Records the ID and name of model types, implemented through the Model_Map table.\nHyperparameter Default Value Management: Records the default hyperparameter values for each model type, implemented through the Hyperparameter_Def_Values table.\nModel Type-Model Association: Records the type of each model, implemented through the ID_Map table.\nDataset Variable Details: Records the ID, name, data type, number of unique values, and number of null values for each variable in the dataset, implemented through the Dataset_Variable_Details table, with each dataset's detailed information linked to a dataset.\nDataset Tag Management: Records the ID and name of dataset tags, implemented through the Tags table, and records the association between each dataset and its tags, implemented through the Tag_Map table.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0347.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0347\nCREATE TABLE `leaderboard_metadata` (\n  `run_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `execution_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `run_time` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `run_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `max_models` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `model_species` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`run_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `leaderboard` (\n  `model_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `model_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `rmse` float NOT NULL,\n  `mse` float NOT NULL,\n  `mae` float NOT NULL,\n  `rmsle` float NOT NULL,\n  `presence_stacked_ensemble_best_of_family` boolean NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`model_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `model_map` (\n  `model_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `model_type_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`model_type_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `dataset_variable_details` (\n  `variable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `variable_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `data_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `unique_values` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `null_values` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `dataset_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`variable_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`dataset_id`) REFERENCES `dataset_metadata`(`dataset_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tags` (\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `tag_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`tag_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `hyperparameter_value` (\n  `hyperparameter_value_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `model_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `hyperparameter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `value` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`hyperparameter_value_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`model_id`) REFERENCES `leaderboard`(`model_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`hyperparameter_id`) REFERENCES `hyperparameter`(`hyperparameter_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `model_run` (\n  `model_run_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `run_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `model_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`model_run_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`run_id`) REFERENCES `leaderboard_metadata`(`run_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`model_id`) REFERENCES `leaderboard`(`model_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `data_map` (\n  `data_map_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `dataset_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `model_run_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`data_map_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`dataset_id`) REFERENCES `dataset_metadata`(`dataset_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`model_run_id`) REFERENCES `model_run`(`model_run_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `hyperparameter_def_values` (\n  `def_value_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `model_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `hyperparameter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `default_value` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`def_value_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`model_type_id`) REFERENCES `model_map`(`model_type_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`hyperparameter_id`) REFERENCES `hyperparameter`(`hyperparameter_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `id_map` (\n  `id_map_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `model_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `model_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id_map_id`),\n  FOREIGN KEY (`model_id`) REFERENCES `leaderboard`(`model_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  FOREIGN KEY (`model_type_id`) REFERENCES `model_map`(`model_type_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `hyperparameter` (\n  `hyperparameter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `hyperparameter_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`hyperparameter_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `dataset_metadata` (\n  `dataset_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `dataset_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `owner` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `license` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `visibility` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_update_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `data_size` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `number_of_rows` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `number_of_columns` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`dataset_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
